<Layout
  title="ERCOT Queue Update, October 2026 — Power Grab TX"
  description="Gas in ERCOT's generation queue jumped 10.8 GW in one month. Seven new Black Mountain-linked gas units pushed Cameron and Freestone counties into the top 15."
  image="/ercot-queue-october-2026-update.webp"
  type="article"
>
  <article class="post-page">
    <img src="/ercot-queue-october-2026-update.webp" alt="A glowing circuit-board map of Texas with three orange-lit points over a city skyline at sunset, with gas power plants releasing steam, battery containers, solar panels and transmission towers below" class="post-image" width="1248" height="832" />

    <div class="post-content">
      <h1>Queue Update: Gas Jumps 10.8 GW in a Month as Black Mountain Doubles Down</h1>
      <p class="post-card-date"><time datetime="2026-11">November 2026</time> · Update to <a href="/posts/ercot-queue-by-county/">Lining Up for the Grid</a></p>

      <h2>📘 Summary</h2>
      <p>Last month we mapped ERCOT's generation queue <a href="/posts/ercot-queue-by-county/">county by county</a> using the September 2026 report. ERCOT has now published its October 2026 report, and one change stands out: <strong>gas</strong>.</p>
      <p>The overall queue barely moved. It went from 1,758 projects to <strong>1,736</strong>, and from 438.5 GW to <strong>445.9 GW</strong>, up about 1.7%. Underneath that, 43 new projects came in and 65 left the list. The new arrivals were mostly gas, while the departures were all solar, batteries and wind.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Gas grew 10.8 GW in one month</strong>, from 79.1 GW to 89.8 GW, a 14% jump. Gas is now about 20% of the queue, up from 18%.</li>
        <li><strong>Seven of the new gas units carry Black Mountain names.</strong> Each is listed at 990.6 MW, adding about 6.9 GW in Cameron, Leon and Freestone counties. These are the same company names behind the Parker County project we covered in <a href="/posts/black-mountain-fact-check/">Fact vs. Fiction</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Two counties joined the top 15.</strong> Cameron County jumped from #17 to #4, and Freestone County went from #21 to #11. Zapata and Lamar counties dropped to #16 and #17.</li>
        <li><strong>Solar and batteries shrank.</strong> Battery storage fell 2.2 GW and solar fell 1 GW. Refugio County lost 1.6 GW when the Ross Solar and Ross Storage projects left the list.</li>
        <li><strong>The queue got more speculative.</strong> Capacity without a signed interconnection agreement rose to 300.4 GW, about 67% of the queue. Capacity under construction held at about 10.2 GW.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>🔥 The Gas Surge</h2>
      <p>ERCOT's October report added 10.8 GW of new gas projects, the biggest net change of any fuel this month. The largest of them are at the earliest stage, with no signed interconnection agreement yet.</p>
      <table class="post-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Project</th><th>County</th><th>MW</th><th>Listed developer</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Ironwood Energy Center</td><td>Callahan</td><td>1,485</td><td>Ironwood Energy Center</td></tr>
          <tr><td>TempleCloud Gas</td><td>Bell</td><td>1,140</td><td>Kalnin Ventures, LLC</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Rattler Combined Cycle Energy Center I, II and III</td><td>Cameron</td><td>2,972 (3 × 990.6)</td><td>Black Mountain Energy Storage II</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Great Rock Energy Center II and III</td><td>Leon</td><td>1,981 (2 × 990.6)</td><td>Black Mountain Energy Storage II</td></tr>
          <tr><td>BM Freestone Energy Center II and III</td><td>Freestone</td><td>1,981 (2 × 990.6)</td><td>Black Mountain Energy Storage II</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ironwood Energy Center II</td><td>Callahan</td><td>743</td><td>Ironwood Energy Center II</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Blue Energy Center, Phase 2b (steam)</td><td>Victoria</td><td>475</td><td>Sister 1, LLC</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Counting every project listed under a Black Mountain company or Fort Worth Power Core, the LLC that holds Black Mountain's Parker County air permit, the company's gas in ERCOT's queue <strong>roughly doubled in a month</strong>: from 7 projects and 6.5 GW in September to <strong>14 projects and 13.4 GW</strong> in October. Those projects are spread across eight counties: Bastrop, Briscoe, Cameron, Fannin, Freestone, Hale, Leon and Somervell.</p>
      <p>The new Freestone and Leon units are numbered II and III, and each sits alongside an earlier Black Mountain filing in the same county. That pattern suggests multi-unit gas campuses rather than one-off plants. A queue filing doesn't say who the power is for. In Parker County, Black Mountain's state permit describes its turbines as power for a new data center.</p>

      <h2>🗺️ The New Top 15</h2>
      <p>The top 15 counties now hold 403 projects and 130.9 GW, about 29% of everything in ERCOT's queue. Gas is the largest fuel in six of them, up from four in September.</p>
      <table class="post-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>#</th><th>County</th><th>Projects</th><th>Capacity</th><th>Change since Sept.</th><th>Largest fuel</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
